From: FlyFish-go <2541290956@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: skip pdev deinit when the radio is already gone

When firmware-crash recovery fails (qmi set mode times out, "failed to
start core"), ath11k_core_restart() still runs ath11k_nss_teardown(),
and ath11k_nss_pdev_deinit() dereferences ab->pdevs[i].ar, which is
NULL by then (first use: ath11k_nss_peer_stats_disable() ->
ath11k_nss_stats_cfg() -> ar->ab). The kernel oopses in the restart
worker and panics. Skip such a radio.

Seen on IPQ5018 (2.4 GHz repeater, upstream AP gone, fw_recovery on):
2 of 15 recoveries ended in this panic.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -4831,6 +4831,17 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_NSS, "NSS pdev %d deinit\n", radio_id);
+
+	/* A failed firmware-crash recovery can leave the pdev already torn
+	 * down; everything below needs ar, so skip this radio instead of
+	 * dereferencing NULL and panicking.
+	 */
+	if (!ar) {
+		ath11k_warn(ab, "nss pdev %d deinit skipped: radio not set up\n",
+			    radio_id);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	dyn_if_type = ath11k_nss_get_dynamic_interface_type(ab);
 
 	/* Disable NSS wifili peer stats before teardown */
